  "id": "nephrogenic-diabetes-insipidus",
  "term": "nephrogenic diabetes insipidus",
  "definition": "Nephrogenic diabetes insipidus is a kidney-related adverse effect that can occur in some people who take lithium. In this context, it is described as affecting about 15–20% of lithium users and as being linked to a higher risk of chronic kidney disease.",
